/-
# Generators of abelian subgroups of finite p-groups (Kourovka Notebook Problem 20.75)

Kourovka Notebook, Problem 20.75 (L. Pyber), marked solved in the 21st issue: let `G` be a finite
`p`-group and assume that all abelian normal subgroups of `G` can be generated by `k` elements. Is
it true that every abelian subgroup of `G` can be generated by `2k` elements?
-/

module

public import Batteries.Util.ProofWanted
public import Mathlib.GroupTheory.PGroup

@[expose] public section

namespace MathlibExt.GroupTheory.AbelianNormalGeneratorsPGroupKourovka20Problem75Wanted

/-!
Source: E. I. Khukhro and V. D. Mazurov (eds.), Unsolved Problems in Group Theory: The Kourovka
Notebook, 21st issue, arXiv:1401.0300v49 (2026), Problem 20.75 (L. Pyber). UnsolvedMath record
UM-00701733 (`KOU-20.75`), dataset ulamai/UnsolvedMath v1.8.0.

Generated by `k` elements: the closure of a `Finset` of at most `k` elements. The question is stated
for all primes `p` and all `k`; abelian subgroups are written by pairwise commutation.
-/

/-- Kourovka 20.75 (L. Pyber): for every prime `p` and every `k`, if all abelian normal
subgroups of a finite `p`-group `G` can be generated by `k` elements, then every abelian subgroup
of `G` can be generated by `2k` elements. -/
def abelianSubgroupGeneratorsLeTwiceNormal : Prop :=
  ∀ (p k : ℕ) (G : Type) [Group G] [Finite G], p.Prime → IsPGroup p G →
    (∀ A : Subgroup G, A.Normal → (∀ x ∈ A, ∀ y ∈ A, x * y = y * x) →
      ∃ s : Finset G, s.card ≤ k ∧ Subgroup.closure (s : Set G) = A) →
    ∀ B : Subgroup G, (∀ x ∈ B, ∀ y ∈ B, x * y = y * x) →
      ∃ s : Finset G, s.card ≤ 2 * k ∧ Subgroup.closure (s : Set G) = B

/--
Resolved false: Muliarchyk (Theorem 1.1) constructs a finite `2`-group of order `2^(110N+1)`, `N =
2124210350`, whose abelian normal subgroups can be generated by `32N + 1` elements while an
elementary abelian subgroup needs `65N > 2(32N + 1)` generators; the 21st issue of the Kourovka
Notebook marks 20.75 solved ("No, it is not"). Source: E. I. Khukhro and V. D. Mazurov (eds.),
Unsolved Problems in Group Theory: The Kourovka Notebook, 21st issue, arXiv:1401.0300v49 (2026),
Problem 20.75 (L. Pyber); resolution: K. Muliarchyk, An explicit counterexample to Kourovka Notebook
Problem 20.75, preprint (2026), Kourovka Notebook site, Theorem 1.1: for N = 2124210350 an
explicitly specified finite 2-group of order 2^(110N+1) in which every abelian normal subgroup can
be generated by at most 32N + 1 elements and some elementary abelian subgroup needs 65N generators;
Kourovka Notebook (21st issue), Problem 20.75: No, it is not,
https://kourovkanotebookorg.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/kourovka_20.75_solution.pdf.
-/
public theorem_wanted abelianSubgroupGeneratorsLeTwiceNormal_refuted :
    ¬ abelianSubgroupGeneratorsLeTwiceNormal

end MathlibExt.GroupTheory.AbelianNormalGeneratorsPGroupKourovka20Problem75Wanted
